WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.034 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-You interned at "SNL."

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got your start doing
a lot of sketch-comedy stuff

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
here in New York.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.841
I did not realize you also
performed on a cruise ship.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, cruise ships
here in New York?

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:12.112
-Yeah, so, there's a boat
that goes around Manhattan

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:15.015
on both the rivers called
the Spirit of New York.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mm-hmm.
-And it's -- I think,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.486
unbeknownst to the people
who just think they're getting,

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a simple cruise
around Manhattan,

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.055 line:92%
it's also a musical cruise.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.924 size:84% position:42%
Um, and so we'd open up
every cruise to, like,

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
let people know it was kind of
a musical cruise

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:29.662 line:92%
by singing a boat-themed parody

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
of The Black Eyed Peas
"I Gotta Feeling."

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:35.201
-Uh-huh.
-And, like, you'd slowly see it

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.036 size:81% position:41% line:92%
dawn in people's eyes.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:39.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Oh, no!
This is a musical cruise?!"

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.306 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.574 size:75% position:38% line:92%
"What have I done?!"

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.943 line:92%
Um, and it was like -- Yeah.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:47.180
Like, I can't hear that song now
without just being, like,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.515 line:92%
transplanted back to that place.

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you remember
the parody lyrics to it?

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.118
-I was trying to think of this.
Okay, I think this was --

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, this is the one part
I remember,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.454 line:92%
'cause we had choreo, too.

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
And keep in mind, like,
we're trying to pump people up

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.792
as they're, like, trying to get
off the boat.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.459 size:75% position:38% line:92%
'Cause they're like,

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't want to be
on this boat anymore."

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:01.861 line:92%
But I think it was like...

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.530 line:92%
♪♪ Tonight's the night ♪♪

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.365 size:81% position:41% line:92%
♪♪ Let's live it up ♪♪

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.133 size:88% position:44% line:92%
♪♪ Take off your coat ♪♪

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪ And rock the ♪♪

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.235 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪ Boat ♪♪

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.437 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.171 size:84% position:42% line:92%
That's what I remember.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.907
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Not good. It's not okay.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:14.574 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It's -- It was fun.

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:18.278
There was one -- I worked there
the Fourth of July one year,

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.680 size:78% position:39%
and I had two songs,
'cause the waiters --

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.881 line:92%
We'd all get up and sing songs.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.617 size:81% position:41%
And we'd have, like,
boas on for no reason.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
And sparkly vests just to be,
like, "Look at me!

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not at the skyline,
which you paid to look at."

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.324 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Um, and there was one --

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
My song was "I'm So Excited"
by The Pointer Sisters.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
And on Fourth of July,
I decided to do,

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a Founding
Fathers-themed one.

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:39.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I was like,
♪♪ I'm so excited ♪♪

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thomas Jefferson.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:41.968 line:92%
♪♪ I just can't hide it ♪♪

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ben Franklin.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.803 line:92%
It wasn't well-thought-out.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-But I got, um...

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.241 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:51.177
-I do think of those guys
as being really excited.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.814 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh! Sick!

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:55.248 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, you've had a lot
of wonderful guest stars

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
on your show.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Any favorites?
Any personal favorites?

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, well, actually --
So, we had --

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
First season,
we had Dr. Phil on.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:04.891 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, and he plays

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:09.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
a figment of my character,
Rebecca's, imagination,

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.730 line:92%
'cause she has some problems.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:14.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
Um, and we'd written him
all this dialogue

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
that was, like,
him talking about, like,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, the reason
that you do this

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.573
is because of your mother
and your father's abandonment."

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Dr. Phil came on,
and he was like, "I'm sorry.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.246 size:84% position:42%
I'll say whatever lines
you want, but I'm --

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:26.913 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I can't say this [bleep]

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.349
Like, this is not what I --
I don't believe in this.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I don't think you should
have an excuse

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.252 line:92%
for why you act like you do."

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "Can I just --
Can I say what I would say?"

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were like,
"Let's do a take

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
of you just being you,
Dr. Phil."

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he looks me
dead in the eyes,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's like --
My character's obsessed

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a person named Josh
on the show.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes,
"Josh does not want you.

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.700 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He does not love you.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.203 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He will never love you.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.771 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You need to move on."

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I, like --
I almost started crying.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:58.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause it was
so real and so true

00:02:58.011 --> 00:03:01.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, so much better
than what we had had.

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.048 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was great.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:05.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I-I had to go back
into therapy after that day.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:05.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.922
-And then we had Josh Groban on,
too, recently, who was amazing.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He just seems like
the gamest guy.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's so --
We made him sing his own name.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:13.960 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At one point,
he literally goes,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.664 line:92%
♪♪ Like me, Josh Groban ♪♪

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Is that the first time

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've been made to sing
your own name?"

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.001 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he went, "No."

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's just what people --
people just do to him.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like,
"You have the best voice.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.774 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Sing your name!"

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Okay. Fine."

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.310 line:92%
-Uh, the show is so funny.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
The songs are so funny
and also beautifully written.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.815
But also, I do want to take
a second and talk about --

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.517 size:84% position:42%
You guys really address
some serious issues.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:40.587
You know, you talked about it
when you talked about Dr. Phil,

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you have a character
who has issues,

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you talk about
mental health issues

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:45.124 line:92%
and, you know, issues like

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.893
suicide and
borderline personality disorder.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:49.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you found it -- like,
the writing of songs

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
a nice way to deal with that
on television?

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.465 line:92%
Because I feel like it's stuff

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
that isn't talked about
that often.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean, I think
it's a nice way -- I think --

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
Songs are not only amazing
joke-delivery devices,

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're also great devices
to deliver an idea, right?

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause songs are kind of
like musical essays.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.312 line:92%
You have your thesis statement,

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is in the form
of the chorus.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you have
your supporting paragraphs,

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:10.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
which are the verses
and the bridge.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.354
And so, it's a great way
to distill something down

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be like, "This is what
we are trying to say."

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, likewise,
when you're dealing with

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:21.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
a serious subject matter,
it's a good way to,

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.895 line:92%
I don't know, get underneath it

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:25.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
and appeal to
everyone's sense of humor.

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.900
Because sense of humor, to me --
A lot of people say,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:31.004
"Oh, it's a musical comedy show
about mental illness."

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:33.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, "How do you joke
about mental illness?"

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:36.809
But to me, sense of humor
feels so emotional and personal

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:40.213
that laughing about dark issues
feels emotional

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:43.283
in a way that it doesn't if we
were just talking about them.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
If that makes any sense.
-It does make sense.

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:46.352 line:92%
And it certainly comes through

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you see it executed
on the show.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.188 size:78% position:39%
I just think you guys
do an incredible job,

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm so constantly
overwhelmed

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
by how many incredible songs
you write

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:53.960 line:92%
over the course of the season.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.761 line:92%
So, congratulations on the show,

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:55.962 size:78% position:39%
and thank you so much
for being back here.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:58.197
It's always so good to see you.
-Thank you.

